---
// Landing page — the Wollack Systems story: who Will Wollack is, why he's
// building it, and how (hustle, networking, and a cofounder found mid-pitch).
// Canonical slate + electric blue Industrial Editorial theme (see DESIGN.md).
// Product detail lives on /journeyman (the "Rust & Iron" variant page).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wollack Systems — Capturing manufacturing expertise before it retires"
  description="Will Wollack is building Wollack Systems to record what America's best machinists know — hands-free — before it retires with them. Meet the founder, read the mission, book a walkthrough."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge capture for American manufacturing</p>
        <h1>American manufacturing is about to forget how it works. We're here to write it down.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Somewhere right now, a plant is calling back a man who retired six years ago. He listens.
          Puts his ear to the housing. Taps it once, with a small hammer.
          <strong>The machine runs.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="lede-strong">
          That $10,000 invoice &mdash; $9,995 of it for knowing where to tap &mdash; is why Will
          Wollack started Wollack Systems: to record what your best people know, without asking
          them to touch a computer, so the plant keeps knowing what they knew.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
            >Book a walkthrough</a
          >
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#founder">Meet the founder</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="invoice-card" aria-label="The famous itemized invoice">
        <div class="invoice-head">INVOICE</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Repair to machine</td><td class="num">$10,000</td></tr>
          <tr class="invoice-divider"><td colspan="2">Itemized, as requested:</td></tr>
          <tr><td>One hammer</td><td class="num">$5</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Knowing where to tap</td><td class="num">$9,995</td></tr>
          <tr class="invoice-total"><td>TOTAL</td><td class="num">$10,000</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="invoice-note">$9,995 was knowledge. Nobody wrote it down. We do.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The founder -->
  <section class="section section-tinted" id="founder">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Who is Will Wollack?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Will Wollack is the founder of Wollack Systems and the voice of Journeyman. He builds the
        old way: show up, network, hustle. Trade events, shop tours, chamber mixers, cold
        handshakes &mdash; anywhere the people who make things gather, the same idea gets said out
        loud: <strong>the knowledge that runs your plant is one retirement from gone.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        He isn't chasing software for its own sake. He's building something real &mdash; a
        permanent record of the expertise that keeps American plants running, captured from the
        people who hold it while it can still be captured.
      </p>
      <div class="accent-callout">
        <p>
          Every company starts as a pitch somebody was stubborn enough to keep giving. This one
          was given at a networking event in Newport Beach.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The mission -->
  <section class="section" id="mission">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why he's building it</h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">&asymp;1/3</div>
          <p>of US manufacturing workers are over 55 &mdash; and heading for the exit together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">800 yrs</div>
          <p>
            of trades, and the transfer method never changed: stand next to someone until you can
            do it too.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">First time</div>
          <p>
            AI can finally learn from a recording of someone explaining their work. But it cannot
            go get it. That part takes us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-close">
        When the best troubleshooter on the floor retires, the line runs slower, scrap goes up
        &mdash; and nobody can say why. The people who know are still alive and still reachable.
        That won't last.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it's being built -->
  <section class="section section-tinted" id="how">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How: hustle first, then the record.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Show up. Pitch. Repeat.</h3>
          <p>
            Will does the unscalable thing on purpose &mdash; face to face. Networking events,
            plant walkthroughs, conversations standing next to the machine. Every pitch is the
            same idea said out loud until the right people hear it.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>One pitch found a cofounder.</h3>
          <p>
            At a networking event in Newport Beach, California, Will pitched Journeyman to
            <a class="inline-link" href="https://etok.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ethan Davidson</a>
            &mdash; software engineer, formerly of Google, now building Wazoo. Ethan signed on as
            cofounder, and now builds the AI that turns shop-floor talk into a written record.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Build something real.</h3>
          <p>
            No slideware, no someday: Journeyman captures real experts on real floors, and every
            record belongs to the plant that paid for it. Wollack Systems grows one expert, one
            plant, one honest conversation at a time.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The work -->
  <section class="section" id="work">
    <div class="container pricing-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The work</p>
      <p class="price-anchor"><strong>Journeyman is the flagship.</strong></p>
      <p class="price-sub">
        Wollack Systems records what your best people know &mdash; hands-free &mdash; and turns it
        into a written, searchable record your plant owns. Journeyman is the product that does it.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/journeyman">See how Journeyman works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="section section-paper" id="book">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The people who know how to run your plant<br />are retiring right now.</h2>
      <p class="section-close-ink">
        One conversation with Will tells you what capture would look like for your floor.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
          >Book a walkthrough</a
        >
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://etok.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Meet the cofounder</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Page-scoped: inline text links inside step copy on the dark ground. */
  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent-blue);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .inline-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-blue);
  }
</style>
